        "transliteration": "Alam tara ilal lazee Haaajja Ibraaheema fee Rabbiheee an aataahul laahul mulka iz qaala Ibraaheemu Rabbiyal lazee yuhyee wa-yumeetu qaala ana uhyee wa-umeet(u); qaala Ibraaheemu fa-innal laaha yaatee bishshamsi minal mashriqi faati bihaa minal maghribi fabuhital lazee kafar:(a) wallaahu laa yahdil qawmaz zaalimeen",
        "translation": "Do you not know the one who argued with Ibrāhīm about his Lord, because Allah had given him kingship? When Ibrāhīm said: “My Lord is the One Who gives life and brings death,” he said: “I give life and I bring death.” Said Ibrāhīm: “Allah brings the sun out from the East; now, you bring it out from the West.” Here, baffled was the one who disbelieved, and Allah does not bring the wrongdoers to the right path.",
