        "transliteration": "Yas-aloonaka maazaaa uhilla lahum; qul uhilla lakumut taiyyibaatu wa-maa' allamtum minal jawaarihi mukal-libeena tu'allimoona-hunna mimmaa 'allama-kumul laah fakuloo mimmaaa amsakna 'alaikum wazkurus mal laahi 'alaih; wattaqul laah; innal laaha saree'ul hisaab",
        "translation": "They ask you as to what has been made lawful for them. Say, “Made lawful for you are good things, and (hunting through) birds and beasts of prey that you train, teaching them out of what Allah has taught you. So, eat of what they hold for you, and recite the name of Allah upon it.” Fear Allah. Surely, Allah is swift at reckoning.",
